WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.437
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.249
A workload in AWS or O C I that holds an
access key is a service account with a

3
00:00:06.249 --> 00:00:08.161
password that never expires,

4
00:00:08.161 --> 00:00:11.987
sitting in a console nobody
in identity governance opens.

5
00:00:11.987 --> 00:00:16.338
This module brings those identities under
the same rules as the rest of the track.

6
00:00:16.338 --> 00:00:20.562
Each one is listed and joined to a
record with two owners and a sponsor.

7
00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:24.387
Every long-lived credential is an
exception with a replace-by date.

8
00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:27.525
And every trust is no wider
than its workload needs.

9
00:00:27.525 --> 00:00:30.733
The program decided to extend
the track to both clouds,

10
00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:34.030
and named the tags that join
each identity to its record.
